WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
(man speaking foreign language)

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.660
- [Narrator] This woman is being scolded

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.860
for being outside without a face mask

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.236
and was chased back into her home.

00:00:10.236 --> 00:00:13.580
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.150
- [Narrator] These people
are being admonished

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.930
for hanging out in a group.
(drone buzzing)

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.020
They were all caught
by Chinese authorities

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.410
who have been deploying drones

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.364
equipped with high-resolution
cameras and loudspeakers.

00:00:24.364 --> 00:00:26.450
(man speaking foreign language)

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:27.283
- [Narrator] It's one part

00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:29.530
of China's massive surveillance strategy

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.680
to tackle the spread of the coronavirus

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.670
which has reached just about
every region in the country.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.090
The virus has infected
more than 80,000 in China,

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.450
resulting in the deaths

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.780
of more than 2000 people in the country,

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.640
far surpassing the death toll from SARS.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.780
- The difference between 2003 and 2020

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.920
is really enormous in terms of
the government's reliance on

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.880
and development of
surveillance technology.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.370
Almost none of these tools
were on offer at that time.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.260
- [Narrator] Sophie Richardson
is the China Director

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.770
at Human Rights Watch.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.920
She says during this public health crisis,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.470
China is embarking on an
unprecedented use of surveillance

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.623
by using big data and its citizens.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.470
So what exactly is China's
surveillance strategy

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.763
and can it work to battle the epidemic?

00:01:18.199 --> 00:01:21.290
(man speaking foreign language)

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:22.230
- [Narrator] There are an estimated

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:26.050
more than 300 million
surveillance cameras in China

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:29.330
and authorities are using them
to monitor Chinese citizens.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.550
- Many of the surveillance
cameras in use in China now

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.790
are equipped with facial
recognition capabilities

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:36.640
which simply gives the
authorities the ability

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.830
to track who specifically

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.180
has gone to which precise location.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.500
- [Narrator] Combine that with data

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.400
scraped from hospital records,

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.260
police files, and public
transportation history.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.560
All that is stored and
linked to national ID cards,

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.080
which gives the Chinese
government granular information

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.370
about all its citizens.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:58.910
In January, a man who tested
positive for the coronavirus

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.850
used public buses and subways

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.940
to crisscross China's
eastern city of Nanjing.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.940
The police posted his journey
with specific dates and times

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.860
on social media with a warning

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.083
that anyone who was in that
area get tested for the virus.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.820
China's public health authorities

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.930
have been candid about the use of big data

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.943
during this public health crisis.

00:02:18.943 --> 00:02:22.860
(Li speaking foreign language)

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.420
- [Narrator] They even
developed a mobile phone app

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.680
called the Close Contact Detector.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.490
The app has a database of people

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.310
who have tested positive or have symptoms,

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.930
so as soon as you type in your name

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.430
and national ID and log in,

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.510
the app will tell you if you've
ever come into close contact

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.390
with someone who tested positive
or if you're in the clear.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:50.130
So far, more than 200 million
people have used the app.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:53.490
- These new and different
uses of technology

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.680
around the coronavirus

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.430
may help resolve some of
the public health concerns,

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.830
but it's also another
way for the government

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:06.840
to gather large amounts of
information about people,

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.200
really, effectively without their consent

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.660
and, in some cases, without
even their knowledge.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.960
- [Narrator] Chinese health
officials say all this data

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.937
is in the pursuit of
controlling the epidemic.

00:03:16.937 --> 00:03:20.937
(Xue speaking foreign language)

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:36.370
- In China, many people
probably have not developed

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:40.508
that kind of awareness in terms
of protecting their privacy,

00:03:40.508 --> 00:03:43.200
protecting their civil liberties.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.180
- [Narrator] Yanzhong
Huang studies global health

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.170
at the Council on Foreign
Relations in the U.S.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:50.640
He says many in China want
this type of monitoring

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.890
because it's about life or death.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.910
- And when they were given the choices

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.200
of protecting their health

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.970
and protecting their
civil liberties, you know,

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.740
probably would choose the former

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.070
even to the detriment of the latter.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:09.420
- [Narrator] Huang says
increasing population control

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.490
during a health crisis
can be a slippery slope.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:16.970
- This widespread use of
surveillance technologies

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:21.290
may also encourage the use
of the same technologies,

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:25.290
surveillance techniques
even after they operate

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:30.290
for purposes may not
be really justifiable.

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:32.860
(pleasant orchestral music)

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.350
- [Narrator] People are also a big part

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.960
of its surveillance apparatus.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.710
After all, President Xi Jinping

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.830
said the fight against the
virus was a people's war.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.720
Authorities send out text messages

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.730
telling people to go
directly to authorities

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.660
if they come from Hubei Province

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.660
where the coronavirus first emerged

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.980
and announcements are
posted all around town

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.429
encouraging everyone
to monitor each other.

00:04:54.429 --> 00:04:56.450
(man speaking foreign language)

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:57.840
- [Narrator] Police patrol streets

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.600
telling people without
face masks to go home.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.410
Some managers of apartment complexes

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.363
go door to door to check on
residents' health conditions.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.430
- This may sort of suggest
that this would be viral

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.990
of these cultural issues we are weighing.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.570
You saw there's people
monitoring their neighbors,

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.950
you know, or even their relatives.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.270
- [Narrator] Some provinces
have started giving an incentive

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:26.196
to monitor family members'
travel histories and health.

00:05:26.196 --> 00:05:28.531
(boy speaking foreign language)

00:05:28.531 --> 00:05:30.691
(girl speaking foreign language)

00:05:30.691 --> 00:05:32.977
(woman speaking foreign language)

00:05:32.977 --> 00:05:34.150
(man shouts in foreign language)

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:36.450
- [Narrator] In Sichuan
Province in western China,

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:39.610
snitching can snag you
as much as 5000 yuan.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.790
That's roughly equivalent
to a monthly salary

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.860
that's more than minimum wage.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.700
One government in Guangdong Province

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.253
is offering 30 face masks in
exchange for snitch reports.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.440
During this public health crisis,

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.170
China hasn't been the only country

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.720
to use technology to track patients.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.500
In South Korea, health
authorities are legally allowed

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.110
to sift through credit card records,

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.430
CCTV footage, and mobile phone locations

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.020
to pin down the travel histories

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:08.370
of those infected or at risk.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:11.190
That information is then
shared with the public.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.040
In China's surveillance state,

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.900
not only do authorities have access

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.820
to more data than other governments,

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:21.030
but citizens have no way to opt
out of that data collection.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:24.890
Beijing says all this is in the
best interest of the public.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.730
- We'll have to be able to see

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.640
how the virus ultimately played out,

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.980
who was affected, who wasn't

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.682
whether the surveillance
technology helped.

00:06:32.682 --> 00:06:35.757
(dramatic orchestral music)

